The user builds Egma voice-agent infrastructure and UX across hosted/self-hosted product code, private Planning, public docs, and `egma-receptionist`. They favor repository-grounded operational proof: inspect actual code and execution paths, distinguish shipped behavior from proposals, and bind tests, review, delivery, and runtime evidence to the same commit. They want compact outcome-oriented plans, exact product copy, responsive browser proof, explicit scope boundaries, and clear separation of normal workflows from exceptional local repair. They work from macOS across multiple worktrees and use Codex Desktop, Claude Code, and sub-agents. For `egma-receptionist`, find and source gitignored environment files in the local main checkout before asking for secrets [ad-hoc note].

## User preferences

- Ground setup/capability answers in current repository behavior and the complete operational path; do not call an adapter, fixture, or proposal production proof.
- “Look at the code!” means inspect implementation and PR diffs before explaining an architecture or telemetry flow; distinguish operator self-telemetry from customer data paths.
