## User Profile

The user builds Egma voice-agent infrastructure and UX across hosted/self-hosted product code, private Planning, public docs, and `egma-receptionist`. They favor repository-grounded operational proof: inspect actual code and execution paths, distinguish shipped behavior from proposals, and bind tests, review, delivery, and runtime evidence to the same commit. They want compact outcome-oriented plans, exact product copy, responsive browser proof, explicit scope boundaries, and clear separation of normal workflows from exceptional local repair. They work from macOS across multiple worktrees and use Codex Desktop, Claude Code, and sub-agents. For `egma-receptionist`, find and source gitignored environment files in the local main checkout before asking for secrets [ad-hoc note].

## User preferences

- Ground setup/capability answers in current repository behavior and the complete operational path; do not call an adapter, fixture, or proposal production proof.
- “Look at the code!” means inspect implementation and PR diffs before explaining an architecture or telemetry flow; distinguish operator self-telemetry from customer data paths.
- For architecture work, research existing seams and comparable primary-source patterns before implementation; when requesting a Planning branch “with all the records” and “push,” keep it committed and remotely synchronized.
- “A much lesser number of tickets” / “THESE are TOO MANY TICKETS” means compact cohesive user-visible outcomes, not component-shaped tickets.
- Preserve explicitly requested product copy; “And do not repeat these lines twice!” means inspect rendered UI for duplicate messaging.
- For substantial UI work, use a numbered route/component/acceptance-proof checklist, one owner per product surface, then one integrated review with focused tests, typecheck, build, and desktop/mobile proof [ad-hoc note].
- Keep planning and public-code commits separate; bind full suite, independent review, PR review, and landing to the same pushed commit.
- During local Egma startup, say whether `egma self-host up` is the normal clean path or an exceptional shared-worktree repair; preserve named volumes and provide concise progress during long builds.
- For “latest origin main platform” / “all the Docker containers are the latest ones,” verify both source SHA and each running container’s image ID, not just health.
- In a named worktree, inspect and preserve existing staged, unstaged, and untracked changes; “Do not commit anything right now” excludes commits and stashes. For a rename, “We do not need to have a compatibility alias” means remove old active references.
- For evidence-sensitive diagnostics, reuse the live Docker stack, correlate exact recordings/spans/timestamps before theorizing, and make production RCA read-only while tracing the exact failed simulation/job; for one run, correlate UI, deployed SHA, logs, and source before a general claim.
- For scoped repository guidance, “very few targeted lines” means a short pointer to one source of truth; check for and update an existing PR rather than creating a duplicate or pushing directly to `main`.
- For security explanations, lead with a concrete attacker request and request flow, then explain the defenses in runtime order.
- When auditing skills, “just tell me the skills. Do not open them!” means report names and delivery mechanics without opening/dumping draft contents.
- Preserve main-task completion alerts but suppress sub-agent completion sounds; check Codex Desktop/UI behavior separately from terminal assumptions.
- For constrained test authoring, honor exact allowed write paths, no-network/no-install limits, and requested machine-readable progress markers.

## General Tips

- Preserve checkout/worktree, authorization, and public/private repository boundaries; re-check live branch, PR, deployment, package, and upstream state before acting.
- Egma self-host normal path: build `@egma/cli`, run `self-host up`, then check web/API health on ports 3101/3100. Shared Compose project `egma` can cause migration/schema drift across worktrees; inspect logs/history/hashes before any local-only database repair.
- Relative-time UI is centralized in `apps/web/lib/instants.ts`; test minute/day/week/month/year boundaries and retain exact `<time>` metadata/title.
- Egma CLI packaging and `npx skills` discovery are distinct: inspect package/tarball separately from public `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` source layout.
- Hosted LiveKit token endpoints need request-time as well as config-time SSRF defenses: public HTTPS syntax, DNS/global-IP and final-socket checks, no redirects, small response limit, and no raw error/body leakage.
- Planning contract: `.scratch/<effort>/` holds `spec.md`, `issues/`, `map.md`, and `research/`; durable context is `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/{architecture.md,adr,agents}`. Run route-closure, Markdown-link, ordering, and `git diff --check` checks.
